    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAASX//1gI\u003d",
        "filename": "keystone/common/dn_conv.py",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 162,
      "author": {
        "id": 8116
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-10-25T16:26:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"this module\" is a bit ambiguous to me, do you mean ldap.dn or dn_conv?\n\nThe only Python module I\u0027m aware of that does dn parsing and assembly (handling quoting, encoding, etc). is ldap.dn. With respect to dn_conv, I know of no library which operates on OpenSSL format DN\u0027s.\n\nThe closest thing I\u0027m aware of some of the very low level API\u0027s in the OpenSSL C library which I think can be cobbled together to produce an OpenSSL format to RFC format conversion utility, but not a conversion in the opposite direction. Plus there are no Python bindings for these API\u0027s. So short answer is I\u0027m not aware of any accepted library that does everything.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAASX//1lM\u003d",
      "revId": "12c5e0d4416f222415f97d44d97155434907c943",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
